firmware/application_intmix.*
    The workload the FI campaign runs. Written for this project; the
    prebuilt image links against the Nuclei SDK BSP, which is
    Apache-2.0 licensed. The SDK itself is not redistributed here.

tb/uart_rx_print.v -- the host-side UART receiver used by the testbench
    Original uart_recv by WangFW (2020-11-5), taken from the tinyriscv
    testbench. Modified for this project: the USE_FILE / LOGFILE
    parameters and per-instance file logging. Both copyrights apply.

tb/chaos_soc_tb.sv -- the testbench
    Derived from the tinyriscv SoC testbench (Copyright 2020 Blue Liang,
    Apache-2.0) and substantially rewritten for this project: the FI
    wrapper instantiation, the scan interface, the campaign observer and
    the UART taps. Both copyrights apply.

host/fi_openocd.cfg -- an OpenOCD configuration file, not OpenOCD itself.
    OpenOCD is GPL-2.0-or-later and is NOT redistributed here; install it
    separately. The FI wrapper speaks the standard RISC-V DTM protocol,
    so a stock OpenOCD works.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
What is deliberately NOT in this repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

No foundry data of any kind. In particular there are no standard-cell
libraries (.lib/.db/.lef/.gds), no memory-macro models or views, no
gate-level netlists, and no .sdf/.spef derived from them. Reproducing the
gate-level flow requires your own PDK and your own synthesis licence; see
README.md and syn/README.md.
